<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Shell raises diesel prices.</title>
<headline>Dutch Shell raises diesel prices.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Monday it will raise its retail prices for diesel in the Netherlands by 0.02 cents per litre with effect from Wednesday.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said.</p>
<p>From Wednesday the recommended price for diesel goes up to 1.476 guilders per litre from 1.454 guilders/litre, Shell said.</p>
<p>Gasoline prices will remain unchanged, it added.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
